{
  "$comment": [
    "The dependency map of the abap2UI5 ecosystem: every repository, what it publishes, whether it is released with the core version, what it depends on and HOW it pins it.",
    "Read by .github/scripts/ecosystem-map.mjs (shape check: npm run check:ecosystem; with --live it asks GitHub and npm whether every pin it names still exists and still says what this file says),",
    "by .github/scripts/ecosystem-canary.mjs (the nightly ecosystem-canary.yaml) and by tools/release-ecosystem.mjs (the ecosystem release).",
    "Facts were read from the default branch of every repository on 2026-11-26. A value that could not be established is null with a 'note' saying so - never a guess.",
    "A pin's 'ref' is what the file names today: a branch or tag for an abaplint dependency (null = no \"branch\" key, abaplint clones the default branch), a commit for .github/deps.json / A2UI5_PIN / a script pin, a version range for npm."
  ],
  "schema": 1,
  "core": "abap2UI5/abap2UI5",
  "asOf": "2026-11-26",
  "kinds": {
    "core": "the framework itself",
    "addon": "an installable ABAP package that builds on the framework (abap2UI5-addons, the extension)",
    "samples": "a sample corpus or a starter template - ABAP that teaches the framework",
    "docs": "a documentation or presentation site",
    "tooling": "a Node tool around the framework (linter, MCP server, playground, protocol, embed control)",
    "generated": "a repository whose content is built from another one by automation",
    "library": "an upstream utility catalogue the core copies from"
  },
  "pinKinds": {
    "abaplint": "a git dependency of an abaplint config: file + dependencies[url].branch (a branch or a tag - abaplint hands it to git clone --branch; null = the default branch)",
    "deps-json": ".github/deps.json: { \"<owner/repo>\": { branch, sha } } - the commit CI resolves a sibling addon at",
    "pin-file": "a file holding one commit sha (A2UI5_PIN)",
    "npm": "a package.json dependency: field names the dependency block and the package",
    "workflow": "a workflow checkout or clone: field 'ref' (null = the default branch)",
    "script": "a pin written into a script: file + field",
    "release": "no pin - it reads the newest release, a release asset or the published package version",
    "push": "the dependency pushes into this repository; nothing here pins it",
    "copy": "a renamed copy, kept in sync by hand - no pin"
  },
